SMT_SOURCE_BUNDLE_DIR identifies an explicit staged service generation source directory.
generationClassSource resolves that directory before embedded definitions, only when the flag is present.
Normal class loading retains existing embedded precedence.
generationSpawnRequest carries the staged source bundle through constructors, blocks and clones.
serviceSourceBundle parses native source, captures current dependencies and replaces its same-name class entry.
Validate bundle limits, sort source paths and hash paths plus bytes for the immutable version identity.
Foreign directories include manifests, source and dependencies; generated glue and binaries are excluded.
Fresh foreign generation startup builds its own staged source version through the existing foreign builder.

Inherited spawn requests read the original source manifest instead of rescanning foreign build outputs.
